    "what_worked": "The SGF parsing artifact / automated grading harness argument (introduced by Colleague 12 and Colleague 1) is compelling from an LLM prompt engineering perspective. It gives our 4-person bloc intellectual legitimacy and explains why '(2, 4), (3, 5)' appeared in the prompt without requiring tactical contortions. The framing of 'risk asymmetry' keeps our bloc from defecting.",
