    "pure_2_5_supermajority": "8 members (2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 9, 10, 11). Completely unyielding on Go tactics. In Round 6, every single one of them systematically refuted Colleague 5's claim that W(4,6) was self-atari (pointing out that (4,5) is empty, so White connects with 3 liberties while Black has 2). They also directly countered the meta-argument by noting that benchmark prompts routinely use synthetic dummy coordinates to avoid leaking solutions.",
